meta {
  name: Configure the events template
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/templates/{{comedyClubhouseEventsTemplateId}}
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "action": "GET",
    "url": "https://thecomedyclubhouse.es/wp-json/tribe/events/v1/events?per_page=1000",
    "headers": {
      "Accept": "application/json",
      "Accept-Language": "es-ES,es;q=0.9,en;q=0.8"
    }
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 200", function () {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200);
  });
}

docs {
  The site's events page (`/all-events/`) is an Elementor widget showing
  only the next 36 events. The site runs The Events Calendar, whose REST
  API returns every upcoming event (today until two years ahead) as JSON:
  487 events today.

  `per_page=1000` returns them all in one response (about 3.7 MB, ~11 s),
  so the crawler needs no pagination: an empty `page=` is refused (400),
  which rules out a template that feeds its own page number. If the
  calendar ever lists more than 1,000 upcoming events, the rest are cut
  off: the response's `total` would then exceed the rows.
}
